{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_11292",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Dermatitis, Atopic through a series of indirect pathways involving corticosteroids. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone is linked to Discoid Lupus Erythematosus, a condition that in turn is associated with Desoximetasone and Prednicarbate, both of which are corticosteroids with similar mechanisms of action. These corticosteroids are known to reduce inflammation and are commonly used in the treatment of skin conditions like Dermatitis, Atopic. The presence of multiple corticosteroid pathways indicates a potential role for Prednisolone in modulating inflammatory responses, which may contribute to the development or management of dermatological disorders. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of corticosteroid use in dermatological conditions, suggesting that Prednisolone may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves anti-inflammatory and immunomodulatory actions, potentially leading to the observed association with Dermatitis, Atopic.",
